383
00:24:30,260 --> 00:27:04,250
The 4 ranks of restrictions (Heaven, Earth, Mysterious, Underworld) were never mentioned before so it doesn't make sense for Wang Lin to know about them. The text explaining them and the Void grade was initially a monologue by Li Yuan.

The sadness of the celestial statue is because the blood of its descendants is being sacrificed before it.

In the donghua, they attributed the celestial slave imprint to the Sword Spirit, and not just a random celestial servant's soul. That way, Xu Liguo is able to help Wang Lin to uncover the scheme. In the novel, Wang Lin figures it all out by himself.

“Not only are you not Li Yuan, even the Li ancestor from tens of thousands of years ago that collected the three treasures was not himself. It was you who merged together with the slave imprint and reincarnated into the Li family!”
“[...]you are driven by a sense of self-righteousness, believing that you must revive your master even at the expense of the entire Ge family!”
“You can cheat others, but you can’t cheat me. As long as it is related to the reincarnation cycle, there is nothing I can’t see through!”
“Even the flesh you’re in rejects you! Because your soul is not of the Li family!”
“What you’re interested in isn’t my Stop spell, but… this!” In Wang Lin’s right hand, the Karma Whip flickered in and out of existence.

